        "id": 5216012
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T08:50:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The share came from a temporary counter in av1_intrabc_hash_search(). For every lookup it counted how many entries of that bucket were in another tile. So it\u0027s weighted by lookups, not by entries.\n\nYou get 3/4 only when the copies of a hash are spread evenly over the four tiles.  For example, take 10 entries in tile A and 1 in tile B. Each of the 10 lookups from A sees 1 of 11 entries in another tile. The one lookup from B sees 10 of 11. That\u0027s 20/121, about 17%.\n\nI didn\u0027t measure how even the spread is. My guess is that screen content mostly repeats inside the same window (text, toolbars, backgrounds), so most copies of a block sit in its own tile.",
      "parentUuid": "48544968_783b8e73",
      "revId": "067cbba72755dd69b0b4f3d75d8c68c8b3234d3f",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "643b6235_c20a46af",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 25,
      "author": {
        "id": 9545
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T00:40:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is unfortunate that once a frame has more than 16 tiles, the number of hash tables abrubtly goes back to 1 rather than saturates at 16.\n\nIs it easy to let, for example, 32 tiles share 16 hash tables?\n\nNote: If you figure out how to do that, do NOT do that in this CL. Just add a TODO comment and do it later.",
      "revId": "067cbba72755dd69b0b4f3d75d8c68c8b3234d3f",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c47fb765_626e9813",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 25,
      "author": {
        "id": 5216012
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T08:50:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think it\u0027s easy. Neighboring tiles could share one table that covers their bounding rectangle. For example, with 8x4 tiles, each table would take 2x1 tiles. The search still calls av1_is_dv_valid(), which rejects copies outside the current tile, so a shared table stays correct. It just has more entries to skip. Only get_intrabc_hash_region() and the table index in av1_intrabc_hash_search() would need to know about the grouping.\n\nI added a TODO in this CL and will do it in a follow-up.",
      "parentUuid": "643b6235_c20a46af",
      "revId": "067cbba72755dd69b0b4f3d75d8c68c8b3234d3f",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
